{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 33e92293, for S3: the celld address item leaves S3. It\nis stated, not built.\n\n1. No authenticated proxy and no new secret. The repository holds no\n   celld ingress source, and a boundary that the kit owns is a new\n   mechanism.\n2. The fact to state: on the Mac kit, Caddy overwrites\n   `CF-Connecting-IP` with the peer's address, so a caller through the\n   tunnel cannot choose it. A process on the host that calls the\n   loopback port directly can. Such a process is inside the operator's\n   trust boundary: it can also read the kit's settings and data.\n3. S3's head says this in docs/security/trust-boundaries.md, at the\n   celld settings, and in the self-host page for the Mac. The witness\n   for this item is the corrected text. No spoof test is owed.\n4. If celld v0.6.3 exposes a peer signal, name it in the note as a later\n   option. Do not build on it in this head.\n\nThe other parts of S3 stand: 2.1, the /health `policy` member, the\nGitHub register comparison, and the kit with hosted MCP closed.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}